LZ4 in Rust
A Rust port of the LZ4 reference implementation.

Reference implementation (LZ4 Library, lib/)
Copyright (c) 2011-2020, Yann Collet
All rights reserved.

Rust port
Copyright (c) 2026, xiaoshaoning
All rights reserved.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Which license applies where
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository mirrors the dual-license model of upstream LZ4:

- everything in this repository today (src/, tests/, examples/, tools/) is a port
  of, or derived from, the upstream `lib/` directory, and is distributed under the
  BSD 2-Clause license reproduced below;

- `cli/` is the port of upstream `programs/` (the `lz4` command line tool), which
  upstream distributes under GPL-2.0-or-later. It is therefore a separate crate
  under GPL-2.0-or-later, with its own `cli/COPYING`. The library crate does not
  depend on it, and nothing in `src/` is derived from GPL code.

The BSD 2-Clause license was chosen by upstream for `lib/` precisely because it is
meant to be embedded in third-party applications; that is what this port is for.

